        "original_id": "a8d728a0-af69-5330-b697-553b22b6b769",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: New York Islanders, New York Rangers, Pittsburgh Penguins, New Jersey Devils, New York Knicks, New York Liberty, National Hockey League, National Basketball Association, Women's National Basketball Association\n- Places: New York metropolitan area, Madison Square Garden\n- Events: 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs\n\nFacts:\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders defeated the New York Rangers in three games in the first round.\n- In the 1974–75 New York Islanders season playoffs, the New York Islanders then defeated the Pittsburgh Penguins in seven games in the quarter-finals after losing the first three games.\n- The New York Rangers are one of three National Hockey League franchises in the New York metropolitan area, along with the New Jersey Devils and the New York Islanders.\n- Madison Square Garden is the home arena of the New York Rangers of the National Hockey League.\n- Madison Square Garden is the home venue of the New York Knicks of the National Basketball Association.\n- Since 1997, Madison Square Garden has been the home venue of the New York Liberty of the Women's National Basketball Association.",
